# Name: Star keychain
# Use: Small stuffed star with a stitched face, for a keychain or bag charm
# Source: docs/sources/Keychain.docx (video: https://youtu.be/jY7pYmuqEeQ)
# Machine support: needs a rotating work holder (rounds from a magic ring); not runnable yet
# Assembly: sew the two pieces together by hand, stuff, then embroider the face
#
# Rounds R1 to R4 follow the source exactly.
# R5 in the source reads: (hdc, dc, hdc, dc) slst in next 3 sts [sc, hdc, dc, hdc, sc],
# slst in next 3 sts * 4. This file reads it as one first point, then four repeats of
# (slst 3, point), then a final slst 3. That gives 5 points and uses all 20 stitches
# (1 + 4 x (3 + 1) + 3 = 20). Check this reading against the video before relying on it.
REPEAT 2 # make 2 star pieces
MR 5 # R1: magic ring, 5 sc
REPEAT 5 # R2: increase in every stitch (10)
INC 1
END
REPEAT 5 # R3: (sc, inc) x 5 (15)
SC 1
INC 1
END
REPEAT 5 # R4: (2 sc, inc) x 5 (20)
SC 2
INC 1
END
HDC 1 # R5: first point
DC 1
HDC 1
DC 1
REPEAT 4 # R5: four more points
SLST 3
SC 1
HDC 1
DC 1
HDC 1
SC 1
END
SLST 3
PAUSE Fasten off this star piece
END
PAUSE Sew both stars together with wrong sides facing, leaving a gap
PAUSE Fill with stuffing and continue sewing the gap closed
PAUSE Make the eyes and smile with thread and sew them on
